Itemize vs. standard
- Standard deduction for MFJ (2024): $29,200.
- Potential itemized deduction you listed: charitable cash $2,000. (You didn’t list mortgage interest, property tax, state income tax, or other itemizable items.)
- Unless you have additional sizable itemizable deductions (state/local taxes, mortgage interest, large medical expenses, etc.), the standard deduction will almost certainly be larger for you.
- Student loan interest is an above‑the‑line deduction and reduces AGI regardless of whether you itemize.

Forms you’ll likely need (federal)
- Form 1040 (main return).
- Schedule 1 (Additional Income and Adjustments) — student loan interest deduction and half of SE tax adjustment are reported here.
- Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business) — report your graphic design income and business expenses, and enter the home‑office deduction (line for business use of home).
- Schedule SE — calculate self‑employment tax.
- Form 8829 — Expenses for Business Use of Your Home (if you use the regular method). Not needed for the simplified method.
