1) Standard deduction vs. itemize (federal)
- For most MFJ filers the standard deduction is substantially larger than $2,000 in charitable gifts alone. Based only on the items you listed, your likely itemized deductions would be small (charitable $2,000; you didn’t list mortgage interest or real property tax). The student loan interest is not an itemized deduction — it is an adjustment (see below).
- Conclusion: Unless you have sizable additional itemizable amounts (mortgage interest, large state & local taxes up to the $10,000 SALT cap, significant medical expenses above the threshold, or other deductible items), you’ll almost certainly be better off taking the standard deduction for federal purposes.

