- Unreimbursed employee expenses (the $780) are not deductible for most employees under current law (suspended through tax year 2025), so they generally won’t help you.

Detailed treatment and forms

1) Standard vs itemized
- 2024 standard deduction (married filing jointly): $29,200.
- Itemizable amounts you listed: charitable cash $2,000. Unless you have other big itemizable deductions (large state & local taxes up to $10,000 cap, mortgage interest, big medical expenses exceeding 7.5% of AGI, etc.), your itemized total will be well under $29,200. So standard deduction is almost certainly better.

2) Wages, interest, investment income
- W-2 wages from Riverside Hospital: report on Form 1040 (Box amounts flow into Form 1040).
- Interest from Citi savings ($1,780) and E*TRADE ($195): report as taxable interest. If total interest + ordinary dividends > $1,500, you must file Schedule B (report payers and amounts).
