- Report gross receipts on Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business).
- Deduct ordinary & necessary business expenses on Schedule C (supplies, software, advertising, travel, a portion of your home expenses if you use home office, etc.).
- You’ll pay self‑employment tax on net self‑employment earnings (Schedule SE). You may also deduct half of the self‑employment tax as an adjustment on Schedule 1.
- If your net business income is large enough, you may be eligible for the QBI (qualified business income) deduction (up to 20% of qualified business income) — rules/limits apply.

4) Home office (165 sq ft exclusive; home 690 sq ft; rent $2,400/month)
- You may only claim a home office deduction for the self‑employment (Schedule C) work.
