  b) Regular method (Form 8829): you compute the percentage of business use: 165 / 690 = 23.91% (≈23.9%). You can deduct that percentage of allowable home expenses (rent, utilities, renter’s insurance, some repairs, etc.). With rent $2,400/month (annual $28,800), rent portion alone = 0.2391 × $28,800 ≈ $6,880 (rounding). Adding utilities etc. increases the deduction.
