- Form 1098‑E (student loan interest) — you should get it from your lender if interest was paid in the tax year
- 1099-NEC / 1099-MISC: include any 1099s you received from clients (report income on Schedule C regardless of whether you received 1099s)

California state forms
- California Form 540 (or 540NR if nonresident)
- California Schedule CA (adjustments to federal AGI) — California has its own conformity rules; many federal adjustments carry over but some don’t. California generally requires reporting of Schedule C business income and allows home-office deductions for self-employed residents similar to federal treatment, but there are differences; I recommend verifying with CA instructions or your preparer.

