Estimated/quarterly tax and withholding notes
- Because you have self‑employment income you are potentially subject to quarterly estimated tax payments for both income tax and self‑employment tax unless your W‑2 withholding covers the total tax due. If tax owed (after withholding) is large, you may face penalties for underpayment. Consider increasing W-2 withholding or making estimated payments (Form 1040-ES) if you expect taxes due.

